SUMMARY:AVL Digital Nomads - Book Club
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\n**October 2026 Selection - *Drive Your Plo
 w Over the Bones of the Dead* by Olga Tokarczuk**\n[Amazon](https://www.am
 azon.com/Drive-Your-Plow-Over-Bones/dp/0525541330/) - [GoodReads](https://
 www.goodreads.com/book/show/51648276-drive-your-plow-over-the-bones-of-the
 -dead)\n\n*In a remote Polish village\, Janina devotes the dark winter day
 s to studying astrology\, translating the poetry of William Blake\, and ta
 king care of the summer homes of wealthy Warsaw residents. Her reputation 
 as a crank and a recluse is amplified by her not-so-secret preference for 
 the company of animals over humans. Then a neighbor\, Big Foot\, turns up 
 dead. Soon other bodies are discovered\, in increasingly strange circumsta
 nces. As suspicions mount\, Janina inserts herself into the investigation\
 , certain that she knows whodunit. If only anyone would pay her mind . . .
 *\n\n*A deeply satisfying thriller cum fairy tale\, Drive Your Plow over t
 he Bones of the Dead is a provocative exploration of the murky borderland 
 between sanity and madness\, justice and tradition\, autonomy and fate. Wh
 om do we deem sane? it asks. Who is worthy of a voice?*\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-
 \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\
 -\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\
 \-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\
 n**Welcome to our monthly Book Club!** We’re a small\, friendly group th
 at gets together for fun\, thoughtful conversations about a different book
  each month.\n\nFinished the whole book? Great. Only made it through a few
  chapters? Still come. Didn’t read it at all but the discussion sounds i
 nteresting? Honestly\, you’re welcome too.\nWe meet on the **first Tuesd
 ay of every month**.\n\nOne of the best things about this group is that we
  keep it relatively small and guide the conversation\, so it doesn’t tur
 n into three people talking while everyone else quietly questions their li
 fe choices. Everyone has a chance to jump in\, share their thoughts\, and 
 explore the book’s characters\, themes\, writing\, and bigger ideas.\n\n
 You definitely don’t need to be a literary expert. Whether you read cons
 tantly or you’re trying to get back into it\, this is a relaxed place to
  discover new books\, hear different perspectives\, and meet some great pe
 ople along the way.
